{
  "company_name": "SiteTrack Construction",
  "industry": "Construction & Engineering",
  "use_case": "Construction project monitoring and completion tracking",
  "space_title": "SiteTrack Construction - Project Completion Monitoring 🏗️",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Construction & Engineering\n\n**Use case:** Production & Project Completion Monitoring\n\nSiteTrack Construction — earned-value and field-production analytics across 20 active projects spanning bridges, highways, commercial, healthcare, energy, and marine work. Project Directors and Project Controls leads use this space for weekly status (SPI/CPI, milestone burn, crew productivity, safety); the VP Construction and CFO use it to forecast EAC, flag red projects, and prioritize recovery actions.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Schedule Performance Index (SPI) — industry threshold: <0.9 = behind, >1.0 = ahead\n- Cost Performance Index (CPI) — <0.95 = over budget, target ≥1.00\n- Schedule variance (days) — negative = behind plan\n- Percent complete (%) — earned-value based progress\n- Crew productivity (work hours per day, crew_count)\n- Total Recordable Incident Rate proxy — safety_incidents per project-month\n- Budget at Completion vs. Actual Cost to Date — EAC/ETC driver\n- High/Critical risk project count — escalation queue size\n\n**Data sources**\n- `projects` — daily production events: work hours, crew count, daily cost, safety incidents\n- `progress_events` — weekly milestone snapshots: completion %, SPI, CPI, milestones completed, project health (Green/Yellow/Red)\n- `milestone_snapshots` — monthly forecast roll-ups: budget at completion, actual cost to date, earned value, schedule variance days, risk level",
