  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports field-production and earned-value monitoring across 20 active EPC projects. Project Directors and Project Controls leads run weekly status with SPI, CPI, schedule variance, and milestone burn; the VP Construction and CFO use the same data to manage EAC and recovery priorities. Project type mix spans bridges, highway, commercial, healthcare, renewable energy, tunnels, marine, and mixed-use — productivity factors and risk levels vary by type.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- SPI = schedule_performance_index on progress_events; <0.9 = behind, 0.9-1.0 = at-risk, >1.0 = ahead.\n- CPI = cost_performance_index on progress_events; <0.95 = over budget, target ≥1.00.\n- Schedule variance (days) = schedule_variance_days on milestone_snapshots; negative = behind plan.\n- Percent complete = completion_pct on progress_events — earned-value progress.\n- Cost variance = earned_value_usd - actual_cost_to_date_usd from milestone_snapshots.\n- EAC indicator = actual_cost_to_date_usd / NULLIF(earned_value_usd, 0) * budget_at_completion_usd.\n- Productivity = work_hours / NULLIF(crew_count, 0) on projects (target 8-10 hrs/crew member).\n- Safety = total_safety_incidents; OSHA TRIR-style benchmark <3.0 per 200K hours.\n- Project health = project_health on progress_events (Green/Yellow/Red); risk_level on milestone_snapshots (Low/Medium/High/Critical).\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - project_kpi_monthly (source: projects) — dims: event_date, project_type, region; measures: total_work_hours, total_daily_cost, avg_crew_count, total_safety_incidents, project_count, max_work_hours.\n  - completion_kpi_monthly (source: milestone_snapshots) — dims: forecast_month, project_type, region, risk_level; measures: total_budget_at_completion, total_actual_cost, total_earned_value, avg_schedule_variance, high_risk_count, unique_project_count, max_budget_at_completion.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. project_id, project_name, schedule_performance_index, cost_performance_index, completion_pct, earned_value_usd).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 projects with the worst schedule performance index over the last 90 days — what's their risk level?",
    "Show monthly total earned value and actual cost to date by project type for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which projects are flagged High or Critical risk this month, and what is their total budget at completion?",
    "How has average schedule variance days trended monthly across the portfolio by region?",
    "Top 10 projects by total daily cost spent this quarter, with crew count and safety incidents.",
    "What is the monthly trend in high/critical risk project count for the trailing 12 months?",
    "Which project types have the lowest average cost performance index, and what is their total actual cost to date?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in total work hours?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(total_work_hours) AS total_work_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.project_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has total daily cost changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, MEASURE(total_daily_cost) AS total_daily_cost",
        "FROM {fqn}.project_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest budget at completion?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(max_budget_at_completion) AS max_budget_at_completion",
        "FROM {fqn}.completion_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Rank project types by avg schedule variance days",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT project_type, MEASURE(avg_schedule_variance) AS avg_schedule_variance",
        "FROM {fqn}.completion_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY avg_schedule_variance DESC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total work hours logged over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT event_date, SUM(work_hours) AS total_work_hours",
        "FROM {fqn}.projects",
        "GROUP BY event_date ORDER BY event_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total milestones completed to date over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(milestones_completed) AS total_milestones_completed",
        "FROM {fqn}.progress_events",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct forecast id are there per region?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT region, COUNT(DISTINCT forecast_id) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.milestone_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY region ORDER BY distinct_count DESC"
      ]
    }
  ],
